e as described above."}]}]},{"name":"maxIterations","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The matrix–vector products each Lanczos run may spend; nil for 20,000 +"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"20√n."}]}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Return Value","type":"heading","anchor":"return-value"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The eigenpairs, in order from that end of the spectrum."}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Thick-restart Lanczos (Wu–Simon) with full reorthogonalization and locking on −A, from a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"fixed start vector; once k pairs are found, a run on the complement of their vectors checks"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that no copy of a multiple eigenvalue was missed. A Ritz pair is accepted when its residual"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is at most "},{"code":"tolerance","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" · max(|λ|, s\/1000), s Gershgorin’s bound on the spectrum; the vectors"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"are then rotated by Rayleigh–Ritz on M, whose values are returned. The dense solver below 64"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertices, or when k is a third of them or more."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"O((n + m) · products + n · k²) time, O(n · k) "},{"code":"Double","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"s for the vectors and n · max(30, 2k +"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"10) for the basis."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"weight","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" gives the weight of the edge at each position, read once per position.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":""},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"smallest"},{"type":"text","text":" is in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0...vertexCount"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tolerance > 0"},{"type":"text","text":", every weight is finite,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maxIterations"},{"type":"text","text":", when given, is at least 1."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"style":"note","type":"aside","name":"Precondition"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":""},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NoConvergence"},{"type":"text","text":" when a Lanczos run spends "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maxIterations"},{"type":"text","text":" products without"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"converging, with the products spent and the largest Ritz residual on the tolerance’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"scale. The dense solver throws as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"adjacencySpectrum"},{"type":"text","text":" does."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"style":"note","type":"aside","name":"Throws"}]}],"references":{"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/NoConvergence":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The error an iterative method throws when it uses up its iteration limit without meeting its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"stopping rule."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"NoConvergence","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"NoConvergence","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"NoConvergence","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/noconvergence","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/NoConvergence","role":"symbol"},"doc://SpectralGraphTheory/documentation/SpectralGraphTheory/GraphProtocols":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols","abstract":[],"title":"GraphProtocols","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","